6	
7	/**
8	 * The centerpiece animated "product screen" for the migration landing page.
9	 *
10	 * A single app-window mock (ScreenFrame) that loops through the real migration
11	 * flow so the marketing page feels alive and premium without overclaiming:
12	 *
13	 *   0. Connect your old server   — host + SSH, one "Scan" button
14	 *   1. Scanning…                 — read-only probes running on the source
15	 *   2. Here's what we found      — detected apps / containers / databases fill in
16	 *   3. One click → migrating     — progress bar with the real worker phase labels
17	 *   4. Migrated & running ✓       — green verified checks
18	 *
19	 * All copy mirrors what the wizard/worker actually do (auto-detect via read-only
20	 * SSH, no DB passwords, installs prerequisites, copies to the same paths, brings
21	 * Docker/compose + services up, verifies what's running).
22	 *
23	 * Motion is JS-driven (a small step machine, same pattern as AnimatedHero) but
24	 * honours prefers-reduced-motion: those users get the finished "running" state
25	 * rendered statically, with no loop and no intermediate motion.
26	 */
27	
